# Build outputs (design-side discipline: state dirs stay out of version control — 2-02 §BR-D5 / Q5)
#
# All outputs converge under the **repo root** build/, in two sides (cf. Android out/host, out/target):
#   build/obj, build/brick.elf|.bin|.map   image (cross toolchain)
#   build/host/<host-arch>/<host-os>/**   host tools (brickie entry ELF + brickie-gen)
#   build/gen/**                           declaration-side outputs generated by brickie
#
# ⚠ Ignore only the **root** build/, not `build/` at any depth (so `/build/`, not `build/`).
#   Reason: a real trap — the fixture `tools/brickie/tests/fx/build/` (input tree of the
#   V-B build family) was **silently eaten** by the unanchored `build/` rule; locally all
#   was fine and `git status` looked normal, but a clone lacked it and `tools-test` went red
#   at once. Any "ignore by name" rule must first ask: might another legitimate dir share it?
/build/

# The tool's own C++ intermediates (previously swept up by the unanchored `build/`; now listed explicitly)
/tools/brickie/cxx/build/


# Python bytecode (created when tool scripts run directly; derived, not versioned)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
